<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103169" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τερμέρειον</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τερμέριον</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακόν, τό</span>,
		prov., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a misfortune one brings
				on oneself</i>, said to be derived from one <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τέρμερος</span> a highwayman, Philipp.
				ap.Sch.<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				509
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Thes.</u>
				11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Or.</u>
				7.210d
			</span></i>; prob. to be restored for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μερμέριον
			κ</span>. in <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Lex.</u>
				11
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τερμερίης</span>
				prob.<i>portentous</i> in <i>Epic.Alex. Adesp.</i><i><span class="en">
				2.15
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ τ</span>., =
			<i>membrum virile</i>, dub. in <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				11.30
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Phld.
			</span></i>).</div>
